  "text": "Veterinary Oncologic Telemedicine - VRCCO\nEMERGENCY\nSpecialties\nBone, Joint & Spine Center\nRehabilitation Therapy\nSurgery\nVeterinary Anesthesia\nOncology\nDermatology & Allergy\nOphthalmology\nInternal Medicine\nExtracorporeal Therapies\nBlood Donations\nNeurology\nAdvanced Imaging\nInterventional Radiology\nSee All\nUrgent Care\nAbout VRCCO\nVeterinary Team\nVisit Info\nFAQ\nMedical Travel\nJoin Our Team\nClinical Trials\nPonch’s Place Food Trucks\nCommunity\nVet Cadets Childcare\nEvent Calendar\nLearning Institute\nDonations\nPet Tips\nStories & News\nResources for Pet Care\nContact Us\nEmergency\nHospital Directions\nUrgent Care Directions\nEmail\nFacebook\nInstagram\nYouTube\nCALL\nHOSPITAL\nURGENT CARE\nEMERGENCY\nCall\nUrgent Care\nHospital\nEMERGENCY\nEmergency\nSpecialties\nBone, Joint, & Spine\nRehabilitation Therapy\nSurgery\nVeterinary Anesthesia\nOncology\nDermatology & Allergy\nOphthalmology\nInternal Medicine\nExtracorporeal Therapies\nBlood Donations\nNeurology\nAdvanced Imaging\nInterventional Radiology\nURGENT CARE\nABOUT\nVeterinary Team\nVisit & Payment Info\nFAQ Guide\nMedical Travel\nJoin Our Team\nContact\nClinical Trials\nCOMMUNITY\nVRCCO Events\nVet Cadets Childcare\nLearning Institute\nPonch’s Place Food\nDonations\nPET TIPS\nResources for Pet Care\nStories & News\nVRCCO\n/\nVeterinary Oncologic Telemedicine\nVeterinary Telemedicine for Cancer Diagnoses\nExpert Veterinary Guidance, From Anywhere\nConnect with board-certified veterinary specialists to discuss your pet’s total oncologic diagnosis.\nSchedule an Appointment\nVeterinary Telemedicine for Cancer Diagnoses\nExpert Veterinary Guidance, From Anywhere\nConnect with board-certified veterinary specialists to discuss your pet’s total hip replacement diagnosis.\nSchedule an Appointment\nVirtual Appointments\nVRCCO-quality guidance from the comfort of your home.\nBook an informational appointment with a board-certified oncologist for more education on your pet’s diagnosis and the best direction of care.\nThis appointment is for existing diagnoses, we cannot diagnose, treat or prescribe during a telemedicine appointment.\nSchedule Now\nOncologic Diagnoses\nTelemedicine information appointments are limited to certain diagnoses: canine lymphoma; canine osteosarcoma (or suspected osteosarcoma); and canine splenic hemangiosarcoma. If you do not fit these categories, please call and we will review your records (decisions are made on a case by case basis).\nContact Us\nTreatment Travel\nTelemedicine cases will be scheduled to work within your timeline, getting you the best care as fast and efficient as possible. If you decide to travel to us for your pet’s surgery, we are available to help you on this journey. We will coordinate your pet’s appointments and help remove the added stress from your travel.\nMedical Travel Information\nThe Benefits of VRCCO Telemedicine\nVirtual appointments give you access to leading veterinary experts from anywhere, offering personalized and informative guidance for your pet. You’ll come away with a clear, confident plan for their treatment. Contact our team to learn more or to schedule your appointment.\nCONTACT US\nLeading Experts\nLeading Experts\nOur board-certified specialist is a leading oncologic expert, offering the best information on your pet’s case.\nValuable Education\nValuable Education\nThe information you will receive about your pet’s diagnosis will allow you to make the most informed decision for your pet’s care.\nPersonalized Care\nPersonalized Care\nIf you choose to continue your care with VRCCO, we will assist you in this process. We want to make it as smooth and stress free as possible.\nCase Study\nKAI’S CANCER JOURNEY\nHearing that your pet has cancer is incredibly tough and may lead you down a path you might not be ready for. For Kai, this meant undergoing surgery, months of treatment, and years of follow-up care. Thanks to the dedicated team at VRCCO, the love of her pet parent and the support of pet insurance, Kai was able to receive life-saving treatment without financial obstacles.\nOncology\nContact Us\nWATCH Kai’s Cancer Journey with VRCCO\nEMERGENCY\n62889 NE Oxford Ct.\nBend, OR 97701\n541-209-6960\nDirections\nSPECIALTY CARE\n62889 NE Oxford Ct.\nBend, OR 97701\n541-209-6960\nDirections\nURGENT CARE\n1820 NW Monterey Pines Drive\nBend, OR 97703\n541-204-1261\nDirections\nFAQ GUIDE\nEverything you\nneed to know.\nCARE\nEmergency\nSpecialty Care\nUrgent Care Center\nBone, Joint & Spine Center\nABOUT\nHospital\nAbout VRCCO\nOur Team\nVet Cadets Childcare\nDonations\nCOMMUNITY\nVet Cadets Childcare\nEvent Calendar\nPonch's Place Food\nLearning Institute\nCONTACT\nContact Us\nPrivacy Policy\nMain Hospital\n62889 NE Oxford Ct.\nBend, Oregon 97701\n541-209-6960\nUrgent Care Center\n1820 NW Monterey Pines\nBend, Oregon 97703\n541-204-1261\n©Copyright 2026 VRCCO. Website by\nZoePDX",
